.TH CCOL_ITER_NEXT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_iter_next \- advance a unified iterator to the next element
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <citerators.h>   /* or any container header */

cmap_iterator *ccol_iter_next(it);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Advances the iterator to the next element by calling the iterator's
own _next_fn callback.  When the end of the sequence is reached, the
iterator is automatically destroyed and NULL is returned.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
it   Iterator variable declared with ccol_iter_declare() or inside
     ccol_for_each().
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns the (updated) iterator, or NULL when past the last element.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
After ccol_iter_next() returns NULL, the iterator has been destroyed;
do not call ccol_iter_destroy() on it afterwards.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_begin (3),
.BR ccol_iter_declare (3),
.BR ccol_iter_destroy (3)
